(II)--a pupil of वैशम्पायन and son of देवरात (ब्रह्मरात वि। प्।) quarrelled with his guru and vomited the यजुस् (s.v.) he learnt; propitiated the Sun god to get छन्दस् unknown to his guru. Pleased with him the Sun god instructed him in वाजसेन्यस्तस् (Yajus अयातयाम, वि। प्।); in the form of a horse;
1: भा. XII. 6. ६२-74; Br. II. ३५. 9-३०; Vi. III. Ch. 5 whole; वा. ६१. १७-19, २१.
a श्रुतऋषि; one of the madhya- माध्वर्युस्; in charge of a शाखा in the ऋग् Veda; recipient of Janaka's present in a contest for great learning;
2: Br. II. ३२. 3 and १६, ३४. २७, ४५-68.
an एकार्षेय.
3: M. १९८. 4; २००. 6.
